---
globs: frontend/src/**/*.{js,jsx,ts,tsx}
description: React/Vite conventions for modular pages, components, hooks, and API usage
---

## Component and Page Structure

- Keep pages in `pages/` and reusable UI in `components/`.
- Use small, focused components; lift side effects into hooks under `hooks/`.
- Fetch data via an API layer under `api/` or `services/`; no fetches inside JSX bodies.

## State and Effects

- Co-locate local state; use context only for cross-cutting concerns (auth, theme).
- Debounce filter inputs; auto-apply filters without an explicit apply button.

## Accessibility and i18n

- Interface must be in French; all labels and aria attributes in French.
- Ensure keyboard navigation and roles on interactive elements.

## Charts and Theme

- Use Algérie Telecom colors (Bleu/Vert) consistently.
- Encapsulate chart config in `lib/chartTheme.ts` and import from components.

## Exports

- Provide CSV/XLSX/PDF export actions that respect active filters.

## File Size Limits

- Component/page hard limit: 200 lines; extract UI fragments to smaller components.
